1) 从告警标签取 cp_code，在 Akamai Control Cente:
1) Take cp_code from the alert labels and drill down by response code in Traffic Reports in the Akamai Control Center to see whether the errors concentrate on one 5xx code or are spread out;
2) Concentrated 504/502 point to the origin: check origin health and the origin fetch path by curl-ing the origin directly;
3) Concentrated 500 suggests a recent Property configuration release (redirect rules, EdgeWorkers scripts); roll back to the previous version if needed;
4) Compare against the origin 5xx metric to decide whether the fault is at the edge or the origin; edge-side problems need a ticket to Akamai.

1) 从告警标签取 cp_code，在 Control Center 的 Off:
1) Take cp_code from the alert labels and use the Offload report in Control Center to see which URLs the origin fetches concentrate on;
2) The most common cause is the origin returning Cache-Control: no-store/private or no cache headers at all; check the origin response headers;
3) If random query parameters are fragmenting the cache, configure the Property to ignore irrelevant query parameters (cache key normalisation);
4) Once the cache rules are correct, watch offload recover; if it stays low, check whether the content is inherently uncacheable (heavily personalised dynamic requests).

1) 从告警标签取 cp_code，在 Traffic Reports 里按 U:
1) Take cp_code from the alert labels and drill down by URL in Traffic Reports to see which paths the 4xx concentrate on;
2) Concentration on a few paths usually means resources were retired or moved; confirm with the business owner and configure redirects;
3) Concentrated 403 means hotlink protection, token authentication, or geo-blocking rules were just changed;
4) Random paths at high volume indicate scanning; configure rate limiting rules in the Akamai WAF.

1) 从告警标签取 cp_code，直接对源站地址执行 curl -sI 复现，:
1) Take cp_code from the alert labels and reproduce with curl -sI against the origin address to confirm the origin really is erroring;
2) Check the origin application logs and load; a surge of origin traffic overwhelming the origin is a common scenario;
3) If the origin is healthy but fetches still fail, check the origin Host header and whether the origin's IP allowlist is missing Akamai's origin fetch ranges;
4) As an emergency measure raise the cache TTL or enable Akamai's Site Failover to preserve availability for users.
